1
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:04,640
What you did today was totally inhumane.

2
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:07,400
In that case, I have nothing to lose now.

3
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,440
I see you've made your choice.

4
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,960
Why wouldn't you sue her?

5
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,040
I don't want to make her choose between
justice and being a good daughter.

6
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,480
- You're fired, Utt.
- You will regret this.

7
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,640
Runch.

8
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,640
I want a divorce.

9
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:24,240
I don't want my love
to keep hurting you anymore.

10
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:27,200
I'll give your mother what she wants.

11
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,320
You can go back to being her daughter now.

12
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,480
- Make yourself at home.
- Thank you.

13
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,280
Is Runch still asleep?

14
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,840
She's at her house.
Why would she sleep here?

15
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,840
What? She didn't come back here?

16
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:46,960
What do you mean?

17
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,360
There's a rumor going around.

18
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,080
Saying what?

19
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,200
That Runch and Neen got divorced.

20
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:09,800
Come on, Runch. Why aren't you picking up?

21
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,280
What on earth is she doing?

22
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,840
Come on. Pick up.

23
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,640
Excuse me. Is Runchlaphat at work?

24
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,520
This is her mother speaking.

25
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:56,120
Why didn't you tell me
you already divorced that bitch?

26
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,600
Can you talk about her nicely for once?

27
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,800
Why should I?

28
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,680
She's the one who made you sad.

29
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:12,360
She's not the one who made me sad.

30
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,760
You are.

31
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,880
You caused all this.

32
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:26,880
You drove the one I love the most
to leave me.

33
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,480
Don't blame me.

34
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,400
I did it all for your sake.

35
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,840
I've put up with so much

36
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,960
and made sacrifices my whole life.

37
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,400
You think this is what I wanted?

38
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,480
For my daughter to stand here blaming me?

39
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,600
I'm not blaming you, Mom.

40
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,680
I'm just telling the truth.

41
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:54,360
Whose truth? Her truth?

42
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:58,480
That woman who tore our family apart?!

43
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,880
Neen didn't tear our family apart.

44
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:05,720
You never accepted that I've grown up.
That's what tore us apart.

45
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,520
I want a life of my own.

46
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,800
A life of your own?

47
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,160
By letting that girl into your life

48
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,600
so she can humiliate me
in front of everyone?

49
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:20,640
Neen wasn't the one who humiliated you.

50
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,160
It's your own actions that did it.

51
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:28,320
I'm your mother,
the one who gave birth to you

52
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,560
and raised you.

53
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,120
And today,

54
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,840
you're saying everything was my fault?

55
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,840
That's not what I said.

56
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:40,520
I'm saying you're the only one

57
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,280
who made me lose the one I love the most.

58
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:51,400
If losing her hurts you that much…

59
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,840
how do you think I felt

60
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,520
when I lost you?

61
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,840
You never lost me.

62
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,760
You're still my mother,

63
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,560
and I'm still your daughter.

64
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:27,240
You just need to stop
trying to control my life.

65
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,560
You want me to stop

66
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,600
and just watch your life fall apart?

67
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:35,600
My life isn't falling apart
because of Neen.

68
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:42,360
It fell apart
because you never supported me.

69
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,600
How ungrateful.

70
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,560
What an ungrateful child you are.

71
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:53,240
That bitch really changed you, huh?

72
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,360
If I had known,

73
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,600
I would've kept slapping her that day

74
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,200
- until I ruined her face!
- Mom!

75
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,760
There's just no fixing you, is there?

76
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,880
Why would you go around
attacking people for no reason?

77
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:10,000
Runch…

78
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,920
If you keep acting this way,

79
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:20,320
you won't get a single dime from me.

80
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,440
And we'll go our separate ways.

81
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:28,120
I don't even want to know
if you're sick or on your deathbed.

82
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,960
I'm your mother.

83
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,880
How dare you?

84
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:36,640
How could you say that
when I gave birth to you,

85
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,240
when I've dedicated my life to you
all this time?

86
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,920
I know you've dedicated your life to me,

87
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:51,680
and I've been trying to defend you.

88
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,480
You only got away with what you did

89
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,320
because Neen respects me.

90
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,560
But from now on,

91
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,000
if you do something to her again,

92
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,600
I can't guarantee your safety.

93
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,800
Runch.

94
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:16,960
Will you really let her harass me?

95
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,680
Mom.

96
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,360
Think about it.

97
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,200
Who's harassing who?

98
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:42,520
You should leave.

99
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,720
And don't come back again.

100
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,000
I want to be alone.

101
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,160
Runch…

102
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,680
Runch, Runch!

103
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,440
Runch, let's talk this out. Runch!

104
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,320
Runch!

105
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,240
Runch.

106
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,480
Easy now.

107
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:20,560
At this rate, you won't
be able to go home by yourself.

108
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:23,840
Then you'll just have to drive me.
That's all. No big deal.

109
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,920
- Neen, this isn't funny.
- Yeah.

110
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,400
Enough. Enough, Neen!

111
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,680
What the heck?

112
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,400
Are you drinking yourself to death?

113
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,320
I'm not gonna die.

114
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:38,960
I'm just hurt.

115
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,480
I really don't get you.

116
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:46,120
If you still love Runch that much,
why divorce her?

117
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,840
Because she always made sacrifices for me.

118
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,920
Ever since she married me,

119
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:58,480
she never got to be happy for real.

120
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:01,120
She always had to defend me, get hurt,

121
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:03,080
and choose between me and her mother.

122
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,000
Neen.

123
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:07,920
None of that was your fault.
You didn't ask for her to be hurt for you.

124
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,880
No, no. Still, I was…

125
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,920
I was the one who caused it.
I'm the reason.

126
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:18,200
If me being by her side
means she has to suffer,

127
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,800
then it's only natural
I wouldn't want to stay.

128
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:24,640
I want her to be happy for real.

129
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:28,160
The kind of happiness that doesn't
come at the cost of being hurt

130
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,240
or being called an ungrateful child.

131
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,000
- Aw. It's okay.
- Come on, Neen.

132
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:39,240
You need to be kinder to yourself.

133
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,880
When love comes
at the cost of sacrificing yourself,

134
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,680
it can hurt like hell.

135
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,120
What should we do now?

136
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,320
<i>Hey, guys.</i>

137
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:07,440
<i>Today I'm showing you a product</i>
<i>that I really love.</i>

138
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:11,920
<i>Here it is. A smooth underarm cream!</i>

139
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,520
<i>Make sure to hit that button</i>
<i>before it runs out.</i>

140
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,600
PJW GLOW CREAM - 590 BAHT

141
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,720
DOES IT ABSORB QUICKLY?

142
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:17,760
I USED IT AND REALLY LIKED IT.
TOTALLY NON-GREASY.

143
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,840
I BOUGHT IT MANY TIMES.

144
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:19,840
NEEN'S MOM

145
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,440
Hello, Pin. Are you with Neen?

146
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,680
Did something happen?

147
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:29,480
She isn't home yet,
and I can't reach her at all.

148
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:33,680
Please don't panic.
I'll try calling her for you.

149
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:37,160
Okay. Thank you so much.
Please do that for me.

150
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,480
I'm worried she'll act on her own again.

151
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,800
Got it. I'll go see her.

152
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:45,520
Please don't worry.

153
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,040
Yes, Pin?

154
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:03,720
Runch. Is Neen with you right now?

155
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:08,440
No, she isn't. Did something happen?

156
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,480
<i>Well, Neen's mother called me.</i>

157
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:13,680
She said Neen isn't home yet,
and she can't reach her at all.

158
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,640
Not at all, you say?

159
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,560
<i>No.</i>

160
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,880
Then I'll help find her too.

161
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,960
If someone finds her,
please call me right away.

162
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:00,920
<i>Sometimes disappearing</i>

163
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,560
<i>is the only way for the one you love</i>

164
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,360
<i>to be truly happy.</i>

165
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:08,320
INSTAGRAM - YOUR STORY

166
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:23,560
SOMETIMES DISAPPEARING IS THE ONLY WAY
FOR THE ONE YOU LOVE TO BE TRULY HAPPY

167
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,200
It was just a fight.

168
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,400
We'll make up soon.

169
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:51,200
Don't worry about it. Don't worry.

170
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:53,800
I'm her mother. How could I be wrong?

171
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:02,720
I never meant for it to turn out this way!

172
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,520
It's all your fault. Your fault!

173
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:13,120
It's all your fault, Peeracha.

174
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,200
Peeracha…

175
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,880
<i>You know…</i>

176
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,920
<i>Ever since the day I decided</i>
<i>to love a woman,</i>

177
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,560
I've known my life wouldn't be easy.

178
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,400
And if it weren't for you,

179
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:54,800
I wouldn't want to keep moving on.

180
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:03,400
<i>I may not be a perfect woman.</i>

181
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,160
I have responsibilities.

182
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:07,480
I have my own world,

183
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,800
which can feel heavy at times.

184
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,240
But if you accept,

185
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,280
I want you to be there
by my side, in my world,

186
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,560
on every good day

187
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:19,000
<i>and every difficult day.</i>

188
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:22,440
<i>Will you marry me? Will you be my wife</i>

189
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,880
and my family?

190
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:39,240
Neen.

191
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Neen!

192
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:53,280
Neen!

193
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,440
Neen!

194
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:56,000
Neen!

195
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,520
Neen!

196
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,520
Neen!

197
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:13,760
Neen! Neen!

198
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:16,320
Neen! Neen…

199
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,680
Runch!

200
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,480
What, Runch?

201
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:30,680
What are you doing?

202
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,160
Why would you do this?
Why are you hurting yourself?

203
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:36,480
What are you talking about?
I'm not hurting myself.

204
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,120
I just…

205
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,760
I just

206
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:49,200
wanted to be in the water where it's quiet

207
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:53,000
so my heart could take a break.

208
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,600
I want to forget everything
for a little while,

209
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,880
at least just to quiet my mind.

210
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Runch.

211
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,360
Can I ask you something?

212
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:48,960
If you could go back in time,

213
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,720
would you still marry me?

214
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,640
Of course I would.

215
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:01,120
I'd do it no matter what.

216
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,640
Every time I have to choose,

217
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,160
I'd still choose you to be my wife.

218
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,520
Then…

219
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,599
I guess I regret nothing

220
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:21,599
about how we once chose each other.

221
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,320
Thank you

222
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,000
for loving me this much.

223
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:44,400
I was always happy
when I was with you, Runch.

224
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,040
I'll love you forever, Neen.

225
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,320
I just don't get it.

226
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,720
Everywhere I apply, they won't hire me.

227
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,280
You really don't know?

228
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,160
Know what?

229
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,080
Remember who you messed with?

230
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:45,800
Ms. Peeracha is
Chairman Thanachai's daughter.

231
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:48,800
That family has strong connections
across industries.

232
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,320
Did you really think what you did
would stay in the company?

233
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,880
So what?

234
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:55,960
Are you saying I got banned?

235
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,920
Not just banned.

236
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,440
Your career is basically over.

237
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,200
You messed with the wrong person.

238
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,840
When you mess with powerful people,

239
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,880
they can get you blacklisted
just like that.

240
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,040
I didn't do anything wrong!

241
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,120
Damn it.

242
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:16,120
I'm not letting
those two women ruin my life.

243
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,560
BOSS'S MOTHER

244
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,160
Look at you.

245
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:31,600
I can't help but feel bad for you.

246
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:37,080
I'm sorry you got fired.

247
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:41,120
I know who was behind it.

248
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:44,440
It's so unfair.

249
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,520
Abusing her power

250
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:50,280
by ruining someone's life
just for her own satisfaction.

251
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,200
I'm having a really hard time.

252
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,960
Everywhere I go, they won't hire me.

253
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,880
I don't know what to do.

254
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:03,440
I have to pay off my debts,
my car loan, and my mortgage.

255
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:09,560
Hey, I understand.

256
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:13,000
This should never happen
to someone like you.

257
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,720
I know a way you can earn money.

258
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:22,880
The question is, would you dare to do it?

259
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,640
What do you mean?

260
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:36,280
Is there anything else I can do for you?

261
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,760
That should be all. You can go home.

262
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,120
What about you, though?

263
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,880
I've still got a bit of work left.
I'll probably finish late.

264
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:53,960
I'll get going now, then.
Get home safe, Ms. Neen.

265
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:55,480
Alright. Thank you.

266
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:30,880
Hello?

267
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,480
<i>I have your daughter.</i>

268
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,560
Who are you? What are you talking about?

269
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:38,960
If you want your daughter back safely,

270
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,760
do as I say!

271
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:41,960
Neen!

272
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:44,200
Mom, let me talk to them.

273
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,720
What's going on?

274
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:51,000
Hello. Who are you?

275
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:52,240
<i>Listen to me carefully.</i>

276
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:54,240
Get me 30 million,

277
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,520
<i>or your sister dies!</i>

278
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,200
Don't joke like that.

279
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,920
No more prank calls,
or I'm telling the police.

280
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:09,640
Did he kidnap Neen?

281
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:14,120
I don't think so. I'll try calling her.

282
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:16,000
Yeah, call her.

283
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:22,440
Hello. Neen? Where are you?

284
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:34,640
On my rounds, I found this bag
and this car key right here on the floor.

285
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:53,600
Dad.

286
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:57,240
Go ahead and call the police.

287
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:03,320
What's going on? Did they find Neen?

288
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:07,840
That call earlier was real.

289
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,640
What?

290
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:11,480
Neen…

291
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:23,400
- Hello?
- Why the hell did you hang up?

292
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,920
You want your daughter to die?

293
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,600
Calm down, okay?

294
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:28,120
Tell me what you need.

295
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:29,920
<i>I already told you.</i>

296
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,120
I need 30 million.

297
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:34,440
But if you tell the police,

298
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,680
you'll get her back in pieces.

299
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:42,880
How can we be sure she's really safe?

300
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,800
You guys sure ask for a lot.

301
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,960
Wake up. Wake up!

302
00:25:57,840 --> 00:25:59,000
Who are you?

303
00:25:59,760 --> 00:26:00,760
Where am I?

304
00:26:00,840 --> 00:26:02,480
Why'd you kidnap me?

305
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:03,920
Shut up!

306
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:09,120
Tell your parents you're okay.

307
00:26:10,600 --> 00:26:13,000
Dad, Mom, help!

308
00:26:13,080 --> 00:26:15,160
- Neen!
- Neen!

309
00:26:18,360 --> 00:26:20,760
Happy now? She's still breathing.

310
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:24,480
But you decide how long
she stays that way.

311
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:29,440
Okay, okay. Where should
we bring the money?

312
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:32,440
I'll tell you that later. And remember,

313
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:33,680
don't try anything smart.

314
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:39,280
What should we do now?

315
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:40,400
What should we do?

316
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:43,120
‪It's okay.

317
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:57,360
We checked the CCTV cameras
near the office

318
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:00,240
and found the suspect leaving the lot
onto a back road.

319
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,480
The road is on a district border,

320
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:04,800
so no BMA cameras are installed there,

321
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:07,640
and the local private ones
have blind spots.

322
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:11,480
So we have no idea where he took Neen?

323
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:15,200
Right now, we can't track
his escape route past that point.

324
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,840
So how will we track him down?

325
00:27:18,920 --> 00:27:21,040
We're following other leads instead,

326
00:27:21,120 --> 00:27:22,640
like phone signals,

327
00:27:22,720 --> 00:27:26,440
driving patterns, and suspects involved.

328
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:33,680
What should we do, honey?

329
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,160
They're taking forever.

330
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,440
I need to use the restroom.

331
00:27:43,280 --> 00:27:45,480
What now? Don't try anything funny.

332
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:48,680
I'm not. I really need
to use the restroom.

333
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,600
I wouldn't dare run away.

334
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:54,800
You sure ask for a lot.

335
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,120
Hello?

336
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:29,160
Hello. Runch, help me! Utt kidnapped me!

337
00:28:29,240 --> 00:28:32,520
Neen? Where are you?

338
00:28:34,040 --> 00:28:35,680
I don't know! I have zero clue.

339
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:38,400
Calm down, okay? Send me your location.

340
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:42,000
Find a place to hide now.
I'll get there as soon as I can.

341
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:58,080
NEW MESSAGE

342
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,560
6 KILOMETERS

343
00:29:17,120 --> 00:29:18,400
Hello, Runch?

344
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:21,920
Neen called you?

345
00:29:26,040 --> 00:29:27,040
Okay.

346
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:30,440
Neen called Runch.

347
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:36,560
Peeracha!

348
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:41,160
Come out! You really think
you could run away?

349
00:29:42,080 --> 00:29:43,160
Peeracha!

350
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:47,320
Come out!

351
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,320
Shit.

352
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:53,680
Come out!

353
00:30:44,080 --> 00:30:45,040
Damn it!

354
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:03,560
Runch!

355
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:07,160
I'm here now. Don't be afraid.

356
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:19,080
Don't be afraid.

357
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:20,680
I'm here now.

358
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,880
Good that you're both here.

359
00:31:28,760 --> 00:31:30,240
This way, I can kill you both.

360
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:53,920
Freeze! Put your hands up!

361
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:55,840
Put them up!

362
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,400
Put them up!

363
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:12,160
Neen. Neen!

364
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:20,640
You're safe now, honey. You're home now.

365
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:27,360
Go upstairs and get some rest, honey.

366
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:48,280
Thank you for saving Neen, Runch.

367
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:52,360
Also,

368
00:32:52,880 --> 00:32:55,200
there was something else
I wanted to tell you.

369
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:00,320
The police called me.

370
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:06,920
They said Utt named Mrs. Gingkamol
for giving the order.

371
00:33:11,040 --> 00:33:13,600
They'll call her in for questioning.

372
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:18,200
I figured you'd want to hear this.

373
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:29,400
Yes.

374
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:36,960
Thank you for letting me know.

375
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,680
But I'd rather stay out of it

376
00:33:40,280 --> 00:33:42,400
and let the law take its course.

377
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:46,640
You reap

378
00:33:47,320 --> 00:33:49,920
what you sow.

379
00:33:55,040 --> 00:33:56,360
Come in.

380
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:08,280
I'm here as Mrs. Gingkamol's lawyer.

381
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:11,440
Please have a seat.

382
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:19,920
For Mrs. Gingkamol's case, it turns out

383
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:24,920
the investigators can't charge her
with solicitation of kidnapping.

384
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:28,440
Utt did name her,

385
00:34:28,520 --> 00:34:30,800
but there's no evidence.

386
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:33,760
No recordings, messages,

387
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:35,120
or money transfers.

388
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:37,560
There's nothing to confirm

389
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:39,600
that she was the mastermind.

390
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:44,120
So legally, she can't be charged.

391
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:46,280
So my mom's off the hook.

392
00:34:48,639 --> 00:34:49,639
Yes.

393
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,679
I knew this would happen.

394
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,480
Are you disappointed?

395
00:34:58,600 --> 00:34:59,560
Yes.

396
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,120
And angry.

397
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:04,960
Not with the law,

398
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:09,080
but the fact that
some people can hurt others

399
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:12,000
without any consequences.

400
00:35:15,560 --> 00:35:16,880
I understand.

401
00:35:17,920 --> 00:35:20,680
Actually, she wanted to speak with you.

402
00:35:21,200 --> 00:35:24,160
She said she wanted to explain
and clear the air.

403
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:27,040
No need for that.

404
00:35:27,640 --> 00:35:30,360
No explanation can undo
what really happened.

405
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,920
Just because she wasn't charged

406
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:36,160
doesn't mean she isn't guilty.

407
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:44,960
MOM

408
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:57,840
Why won't she pick up? It's been days!

409
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:00,320
Honey, look.

410
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:03,440
Runch has been ignoring my calls for days.
What's going on?

411
00:36:03,520 --> 00:36:06,320
Do you really not know
why she's like that?

412
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:08,880
What's that supposed to mean?
I didn't do anything wrong.

413
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:11,320
Can't you see?
Even the police can't arrest me.

414
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:15,160
Sure, you weren't charged with anything.

415
00:36:15,760 --> 00:36:17,800
Exactly. So I'm not guilty.

416
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:21,000
But you know full well what the truth is.

417
00:36:22,240 --> 00:36:23,480
What are you implying?

418
00:36:24,280 --> 00:36:26,560
I'm not guilty. Don't accuse me.

419
00:36:26,640 --> 00:36:28,560
I'm not accusing you.

420
00:36:28,640 --> 00:36:30,880
I just choose not to lie to myself,
unlike you.

421
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:32,760
You want me to go to jail that bad?

422
00:36:32,840 --> 00:36:35,920
Yes. If it will set you straight.

423
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,520
At least it will stop you
from hurting others,

424
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:40,680
especially our daughter!

425
00:36:40,760 --> 00:36:42,680
- But I--
- Enough!

426
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,760
Stop bothering Runch.

427
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:48,360
She's suffered enough already.

428
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:04,800
No. I did nothing wrong.

429
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:06,880
Absolutely not.

430
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:26,560
Gingkamol's off the hook?

431
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:32,600
Really?

432
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:34,760
That's not fair at all, Dad.

433
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:36,200
What she did was serious.

434
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:37,920
She had someone kidnapped for ransom,

435
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:39,480
yet she's off the hook?

436
00:37:39,560 --> 00:37:41,040
Wouldn't that encourage her?

437
00:37:45,120 --> 00:37:47,480
Can't we do anything to someone like her?

438
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:54,280
If the law can't punish someone like her,

439
00:37:55,480 --> 00:37:57,320
then we'll leave it to karma.

440
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:59,280
Sooner or later,

441
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:02,440
she'll get her karma
for what she did to us.

442
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:15,960
Ungrateful daughter.

443
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:31,680
Hello?

444
00:38:31,760 --> 00:38:33,800
<i>Hello, Mrs. Gingkamol.</i>

445
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:36,200
<i>I'm calling from</i>
<i>the VIP Customer Care team</i>

446
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,960
<i>at the bank where you hold</i>
<i>your fixed deposit account.</i>

447
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:41,040
<i>Is everything alright?</i>

448
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:43,800
<i>I have a quick special offer</i>
<i>I'd love to share.</i>

449
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:48,200
<i>We have a new investment product</i>
<i>that offers returns several times higher</i>

450
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:50,880
<i>than what you're earning</i>
<i>on your fixed deposit interest.</i>

451
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:55,760
<i>If you're interested, your money can grow</i>
<i>significantly in just a few months</i>

452
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:59,360
<i>without the risks of the stock market,</i>
<i>and it's completely hassle-free.</i>

453
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:02,720
- Sounds too good to be true.
<i>- But,</i>

454
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:07,040
I can assure you, this offer
is reserved for our VIP customers,

455
00:39:07,120 --> 00:39:09,880
<i>and you're the first person</i>
<i>I chose to call.</i>

456
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,440
What will I have to do?

457
00:39:12,040 --> 00:39:15,640
<i>It's very simple, actually.</i>
<i>I'll message you the details.</i>

458
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:19,280
<i>You'll just have to verify your identity</i>
<i>and transfer the money from your account</i>

459
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:21,280
<i>to an investment account.</i>

460
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:24,560
In that case, please send me the details.

461
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:27,520
DIVORCE AGREEMENT

462
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,760
SIGNATURE - RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM
SIGNATURE - PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL

463
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:43,280
Still undecided?

464
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:49,280
This isn't easy at all, Dad.

465
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:53,760
I don't mean to rush your decision.

466
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:56,600
I just want you

467
00:39:57,240 --> 00:39:58,920
to listen to your heart.

468
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:04,360
Will you really be fine

469
00:40:05,640 --> 00:40:07,680
with having to be extra careful,

470
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:11,640
never knowing when
someone will hurt you again?

471
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:16,880
I'm not mad at Runch, though.

472
00:40:19,600 --> 00:40:21,000
I'm sure

473
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:24,200
she's just as hurt as I am.

474
00:40:28,200 --> 00:40:29,240
I know.

475
00:40:30,320 --> 00:40:32,000
I'm not mad at her either.

476
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:37,840
But I'm your father.

477
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:43,640
I can't stand seeing my daughter
get hurt anymore,

478
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:47,880
whether it's intentional or not.

479
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:06,600
BOTH OF THE SPOUSES HAVE READ
AND UNDERSTOOD ALL OF THE ABOVE CONDITIONS

480
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:16,360
SIGNATURE
RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM - SPOUSE 1

481
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:18,440
SIGNATURE
PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL - SPOUSE 2

482
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:33,000
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE - THIS CERTIFIES THAT

483
00:41:33,080 --> 00:41:35,440
MISS RUNCHLAPHAT AND MISS PEERACHA
HAVE REGISTERED THEIR MARRIAGE

484
00:41:50,960 --> 00:41:52,560
Guess it's time now.

485
00:42:20,040 --> 00:42:22,920
LAST YEAR

486
00:42:29,240 --> 00:42:30,400
Neen!

487
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:32,360
Neen.

488
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,000
‪Let me see.

489
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:37,880
Come on.

490
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:40,280
Let's get you patched up.

491
00:42:57,360 --> 00:42:59,000
I'll clean it up for you.

492
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:11,600
This might sting a bit.

493
00:43:13,120 --> 00:43:16,800
Seeing you hurt hurts me more.

494
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:25,440
Can you blow on it?

495
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:36,720
All done.

496
00:43:41,840 --> 00:43:42,960
‪Come on.

497
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:00,160
All done now?

498
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,760
Almost. Here.

499
00:44:03,280 --> 00:44:04,840
The last step.

500
00:44:29,240 --> 00:44:31,320
If something were to happen to you,

501
00:44:32,600 --> 00:44:34,640
I wouldn't be able to go on.

502
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:53,920
This is where we started,

503
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:55,520
so I wanted us to end things here.

504
00:44:55,600 --> 00:44:57,520
No matter what our relationship is,

505
00:44:57,600 --> 00:45:00,640
you're the best thing in my life.

506
00:45:00,720 --> 00:45:02,400
<i>Same here.</i>

507
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:11,360
I never imagined
I'd get to be here either.

508
00:45:11,960 --> 00:45:15,440
Who knows? You might
get back together with Neen

509
00:45:15,520 --> 00:45:17,200
and end up remarrying.

510
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:21,080
If that ever happens… that'd be great.

511
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:07,720
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
